-- EU AI Act, Article 3: the definitions the reporting rules use.
-- DRAFT. Not for use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Article 3 is in Chapter I, which applies from 2 February 2025 (Article
-- 113(a)), before any scoped duty, so the definitions carry no date of their own.
-- Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 amends Article 3 only at points (14), (14a) and
-- (14b), none of which these rules use.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-domain`

§ `Article 3: definitions`

§§ `Article 3(3): provider`

-- src:441 | ‘provider’ means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body that develops an AI system or a general-purpose AI model or that has an AI system or a general-purpose AI model developed and places it on the market or puts the AI system into service under its own name or trademark, whether for payment or free of charge;
@ref Article 3, point (3) (src:441)
GIVEN s IS AN `AI system facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`I am the provider of the AI system` s MEANS
        s's `I develop the system or have it developed`
    AND s's `I place the system on the market or put it into service`
    AND s's `the system carries my own name or trademark`

-- For a model the text says "places it on the market"; "puts ... into
-- service" is said of the AI system only.
@ref Article 3, point (3) (src:441)
GIVEN m IS A `model facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`I am the provider of the model` m MEANS
        m's `I develop the model or have it developed`
    AND m's `I place the model on the market under my own name or trademark`

§§ `Article 3(49): serious incident`

-- src:537 | ‘serious incident’ means an incident or malfunctioning of an AI system that directly or indirectly leads to any of the following:
-- src:538 | (a)
-- src:539 | the death of a person, or serious harm to a person’s health;
-- src:540 | (b)
-- src:541 | a serious and irreversible disruption of the management or operation of critical infrastructure;
-- src:542 | (c)
-- src:543 | the infringement of obligations under Union law intended to protect fundamental rights;
-- src:544 | (d)
-- src:545 | serious harm to property or the environment;
@ref Article 3, point (49)(a) (src:537-539)
GIVEN i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`point (a): death or serious harm to health` i MEANS
        i's `it led, directly or indirectly, to the death of a person`
    OR  i's `it led, directly or indirectly, to serious harm to the health of a person`

-- "Critical infrastructure" is defined by reference to Directive (EU)
-- 2022/2557 (Article 3(62)), which is not deposited; it is asked as a fact.
@ref Article 3, point (49)(b) (src:540-541)
GIVEN i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`point (b): disruption of critical infrastructure` i MEANS
    i's `it led, directly or indirectly, to a serious and irreversible disruption of critical infrastructure`

@ref Article 3, point (49)(c) (src:542-543)
GIVEN i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`point (c): infringement of fundamental-rights obligations` i MEANS
    i's `it led, directly or indirectly, to an infringement of Union-law obligations protecting fundamental rights`

@ref Article 3, point (49)(d) (src:544-545)
GIVEN i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`point (d): serious harm to property or the environment` i MEANS
    i's `it led, directly or indirectly, to serious harm to property or the environment`

@ref Article 3, point (49) (src:537-545)
GIVEN i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the incident is a serious incident` i MEANS
        i's `it is an incident or malfunctioning of the AI system`
    AND (   `point (a): death or serious harm to health` i
         OR `point (b): disruption of critical infrastructure` i
         OR `point (c): infringement of fundamental-rights obligations` i
         OR `point (d): serious harm to property or the environment` i)

§§ `Article 3(61): widespread infringement`

-- src:569 | ‘widespread infringement’ means any act or omission contrary to Union law protecting the interest of individuals, which:
-- src:570 | (a)
-- src:571 | has harmed or is likely to harm the collective interests of individuals residing in at least two Member States other than the Member State in which:
-- src:572 | (i)
-- src:573 | the act or omission originated or took place;
-- src:574 | (ii)
-- src:575 | the provider concerned, or, where applicable, its authorised representative is located or established; or
-- src:576 | (iii)
-- src:577 | the deployer is established, when the infringement is committed by the deployer;
-- src:578 | (b)
-- src:579 | has caused, causes or is likely to cause harm to the collective interests of individuals and has common features, including the same unlawful practice or the same interest being infringed, and is occurring concurrently, committed by the same operator, in at least three Member States;
-- The provider counts the "other" Member States itself; which Member State is
-- excluded when (i), (ii) and (iii) name different ones is FORK F6.
@ref Article 3, point (61)(a) (src:569-577)
GIVEN i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`point (61)(a): harm in at least two other Member States` i MEANS
    i's `the number of other Member States whose residents it harmed or is likely to harm` AT LEAST 2

@ref Article 3, point (61)(b) (src:578-579)
GIVEN i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`point (61)(b): common features, concurrently, same operator, at least three Member States` i MEANS
        i's `it has common features, such as the same unlawful practice or interest infringed`
    AND i's `it is committed by the same operator`
    AND i's `the number of Member States in which it is occurring concurrently` AT LEAST 3

@ref Article 3, point (61) (src:569-579)
GIVEN i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the incident is a widespread infringement` i MEANS
        i's `it is an act or omission contrary to Union law protecting the interest of individuals`
    AND (   `point (61)(a): harm in at least two other Member States` i
         OR `point (61)(b): common features, concurrently, same operator, at least three Member States` i)
